      "html": "<div class=\"story-inner\"><p class=\"story-eyebrow\">Beside the others</p><h2 class=\"story-h2\">Do you pay for seats nobody opens?</h2><p class=\"story-text\">Most tools charge every month for every person on the account. That includes the office, and the person who does one check a year. Quickler charges for each phone number on the account, not for each person.</p><div class=\"story-article-body\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Your team</th><th>Who inspects</th><th>Quickler</th><th>A per-seat app</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>10 people</td><td>2 regularly</td><td><strong>&pound;150</strong></td><td>&pound;190 to &pound;240</td></tr>\n<tr><td>20 people</td><td>5 regularly</td><td><strong>&pound;375</strong></td><td>&pound;380 to &pound;480</td></tr>\n<tr><td>30 people</td><td>5 regularly</td><td><strong>&pound;375</strong></td><td>&pound;570 to &pound;720</td></tr>\n<tr><td>50 people</td><td>6 regularly</td><td><strong>&pound;450</strong></td><td>&pound;950 to &pound;1,200</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Per-seat prices use the &pound;19 to &pound;24 a seat that the better-known apps publish. All prices are per month.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">To be fair, if nearly everyone inspects most days, a per-seat app can cost less. Quickler suits a firm where many people need to see the reports and only a few do the walking.</p></div>"
